{
 "lesson": "s3-relatives",
 "scenes": [
  "hero",
  "c01-title",
  "c01-table",
  "c01-cols",
  "c01-tip",
  "c01-rule",
  "c02-title",
  "c02-ex",
  "c02-tip",
  "c03-title",
  "c03-ex",
  "c03-tips",
  "c04-title",
  "c04-ex",
  "c05-title",
  "c05-ex",
  "c05-tip",
  "c06-title",
  "c06-forms",
  "summary"
 ],
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "hero-01",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Relative pronouns. The one who, the thing which.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-02",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In English we say: the student who passed.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-03",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here, the little word, who, joins the noun to a short clause about it. It is a relative pronoun.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-04",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In Arabic, a relative pronoun is fixed. Its ending does not change. The only exception is a pair of words for two. They come in chapter six.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-05",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And it never stands alone. A clause always comes after it.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-01",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter one. The table to learn.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-01",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here are the relatives to learn by heart.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-02",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The first one is for one male, or one masculine thing.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-03",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-04",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The student who passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-05",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-06",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The second one is for one female, or one feminine thing.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-07",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّتِي",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-08",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The girl who passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-09",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الْبِنْتُ الَّتِي نَجَحَتْ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-10",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The third one is for a group of males.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-11",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِينَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-12",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The students who passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-13",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الطُّلَّابُ الَّذِينَ نَجَحُوا",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-14",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The last row is for a group of females. It has two words, and both are correct.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-15",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّاتِي",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-16",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّوَاتِي",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-17",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The women who passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-18",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "النِّسَاءُ اللَّاتِي نَجَحْنَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-table-19",
   "scene": "c01-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In every example, the relative comes right after the noun.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-01",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Next, two relatives that are general. No noun comes before them.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-02",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The first means the one who. It is for people.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "col:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-03",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَنْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-04",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The one who passed came.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-05",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَاءَ مَنْ نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-06",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The second means what. It is for things.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "col:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-07",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-08",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "I read what the teacher wrote.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-09",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "قَرَأْتُ مَا كَتَبَ الْمُدَرِّسُ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-01",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A tip on spelling. These three are written with a single L, with a shadda on it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-02",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-03",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّتِي",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-04",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِينَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-05",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The two words for a group of females are written with the L twice.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:written with two"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-06",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّاتِي",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-07",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّوَاتِي",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-01",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Now the rule. All of these are fixed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-02",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Look at the word for a group of males.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-03",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِينَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-04",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It ends like a plural. But it never changes.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "hl:never changes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-05",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In rafʿ, in naṣb and in jarr, it stays the same.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-06",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِينَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-07",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And these two always end in a long ī sound.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:always end in a long ī"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-08",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-rule-09",
   "scene": "c01-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّتِي",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-01",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter two. A relative needs a clause after it.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-02",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This word alone means nothing.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-03",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-04",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The one who did what? We wait for more.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-05",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The clause after it completes its meaning. This clause is called the ṣila.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-06",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "صِلَةٌ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-01",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "First. The student who passed came.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-02",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَاءَ الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-03",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The ṣila is just the verb. It means he passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-04",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-05",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Second. This is the girl who wrote the lesson.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-06",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "هَذِهِ هِيَ الْبِنْتُ الَّتِي كَتَبَتِ الدَّرْسَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-07",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The ṣila means she wrote the lesson.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-08",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَتِ الدَّرْسَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-09",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Third. The book which is on the desk is new.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-10",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الْكِتَابُ الَّذِي عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ جَدِيدٌ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-11",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here the ṣila has no verb. It is a place phrase: on the desk.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:3",
    "hl:a place phrase"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-12",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-13",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Fourth. The men who sat in the mosque went out.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-14",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "خَرَجَ الرِّجَالُ الَّذِينَ جَلَسُوا فِي الْمَسْجِدِ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-15",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The ṣila means they sat in the mosque.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-ex-16",
   "scene": "c02-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَلَسُوا فِي الْمَسْجِدِ",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "ar:7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-01",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A tip. The ṣila has a small link back to the noun.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show",
    "hl:a small link back to the noun"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-02",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Often the link is hidden in the verb.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-03",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-04",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This verb means he passed. The hidden he is the student.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-05",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Sometimes the link is an attached pronoun. The student whose house is near.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-06",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي بَيْتُهُ قَرِيبٌ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-07",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The small ending on house means his. It points back to the student.",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-01",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter three. Choose by the noun before it.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-02",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A relative works like an adjective. It follows a noun with al.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-03",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And it matches that noun. Male or female. One or a group.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-01",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The boy who is in the house.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-02",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الْوَلَدُ الَّذِي فِي الْبَيْتِ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-03",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The boy is one male. So we choose this one.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-04",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-05",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The watch which is on the bed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-06",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "السَّاعَةُ الَّتِي عَلَى السَّرِيرِ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-07",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The word for watch is feminine.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-08",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "السَّاعَةُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-09",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is a thing, but a feminine one. So we choose this one.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-10",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّتِي",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-11",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The boys who went out.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-12",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الْأَوْلَادُ الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-13",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A group of males. So we choose this one.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-14",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِينَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-15",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The women who went out.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-16",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "النِّسَاءُ اللَّاتِي خَرَجْنَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-17",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A group of females. So we choose this one.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-ex-18",
   "scene": "c03-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّاتِي",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "ar:8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-01",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Two tips. First, look at the verb in the ṣila too. It matches the relative.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show:1",
    "hl:It matches the relative"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-02",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For one male, the verb means he went out.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-03",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي خَرَجَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-04",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For one female, she went out.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-05",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّتِي خَرَجَتْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-06",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For a group of males, they went out.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-07",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-08",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "For a group of females, the verb has its own ending.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-09",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّاتِي خَرَجْنَ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-10",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Second. After a noun without al, Arabic leaves the relative out.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show:2",
    "hl:leaves the relative out"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-11",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A student who passed came.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-12",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَاءَ طَالِبٌ نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-13",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here student has no al. So no relative comes after it.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tips-14",
   "scene": "c03-tips",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In English we still say who. In Arabic, the clause comes straight after the noun.",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-01",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter four.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-02",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَنْ",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-03",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "and",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-04",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَا",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-05",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Question or relative?",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-06",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "These two words are also question words. You learn them as question words in unit five.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-07",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So how do we tell them apart? Look at the sentence.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-08",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A question ends in a question mark.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-09",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A relative sits inside a normal sentence. It means the one who, or what.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-01",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Who passed?",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-02",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَنْ نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-03",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It ends in a question mark. So this is a question.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "note:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-04",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The one who passed came.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-05",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَاءَ مَنْ نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-06",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This is a normal sentence. So the word is a relative here. It means the one who.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-07",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Its ṣila is the verb. It means he passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-08",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-09",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "What is on the desk?",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-10",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَا عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-11",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Again, a question mark. So it is a question.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "note:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-12",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Read what is on the desk.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-13",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اِقْرَأْ مَا عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-ex-14",
   "scene": "c04-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This is an order, with no question mark. So the word is a relative here. It means what.",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "note:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-01",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter five. Its place in the sentence.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-02",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A relative after a noun works like an adjective.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-03",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "An adjective copies the ending of its noun. But a relative is fixed. It cannot copy the ending.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-title-04",
   "scene": "c05-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So it copies the place of the noun before it: rafʿ, naṣb or jarr. Its ending does not change.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-01",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The student who passed came.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-02",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَاءَ الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-03",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The student is the doer. It is rafʿ, with damma.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-04",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الطَّالِبُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-05",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So the relative is in the place of rafʿ.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:in the place of rafʿ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-06",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-07",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The principal thanked the student who passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-08",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "شَكَرَ الْمُدِيرُ الطَّالِبَ الَّذِي نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-09",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Now the student is the object. It is naṣb, with fatha.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-10",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الطَّالِبَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-11",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So the relative is in the place of naṣb. Its ending stays the same.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:in the place of naṣb"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-12",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-13",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "I went to the student who passed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-14",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى الطَّالِبِ الَّذِي نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-15",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Now the student comes after a preposition. It is jarr, with kasra.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-16",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الطَّالِبِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-17",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So the relative is in the place of jarr. Again, its ending stays the same.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:in the place of jarr"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-ex-18",
   "scene": "c05-ex",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "الَّذِي",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": [
    "ar:8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-01",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A tip. The two general relatives stand alone.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-02",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَنْ",
   "pause": 0.35,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-03",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-04",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Stand alone means only that no noun comes before them. A ṣila still comes after them.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-05",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "With no noun to copy, they have their own job.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:they have their own job"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-06",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The one who passed came.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-07",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "جَاءَ مَنْ نَجَحَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "ar:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-08",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Who came?",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-09",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The one who passed. So this word is the doer.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-10",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَنْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "ar:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c05-tip-11",
   "scene": "c05-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The doer takes rafʿ. This word is fixed, so it is in the place of rafʿ.",
   "pause": 0.8,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-title-01",
   "scene": "c06-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter six. Not fixed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-title-02",
   "scene": "c06-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّذَانِ",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ar:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-title-03",
   "scene": "c06-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "and",
   "pause": 0.2,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-title-04",
   "scene": "c06-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اللَّتَانِ",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": [
    "ar:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-forms-01",
   "scene": "c06-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Careful. Two more relatives mean the two who. And these words change.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c06-forms-02",
   "scene": "c06-forms",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This one is for two males.",
